<p class="lt-chem-55839">The Z-average molecular weight (M<sub>z</sub>) is measured in some sedimentation equilibrium experiments. M<sub>z</sub> isn&rsquo;t common technique for molecular weight of polymers. The molar mass depends on size and mass of the molecules. The ultra centrifugation techniques employ to determine M<sub>z</sub>. M<sub>z</sub> emphasizes large particles and it defines the EQ, where M<sub>i</sub> is molecular weight and N<sub>i</sub> is number of molecules.</p>

<p class="lt-chem-55839">\[ M_{W} =\frac{\Sigma N_{i} M_{i}^{3}}{\Sigma N_{i} M{i}^{2}}  \nonumber \]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-55839">Consider the polymer described in the previous problem.</p>

<p class="lt-chem-55839"><img data-media-type="image/jpg" data-print-width="4.5in" width="500" class="internal" alt="Eq29.jpg" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/418396/Eq29.jpg?revision=1" /></p>

